## Admin inbound email alerts (company mailbox — learned 2026-09)

**Purpose:** When a customer submits Contact / Bespoke / order / newsletter / community / fundraising, Resend emails the **company notification address** so staff off-site still see the event (dashboard optional).

**Wiring (do not remove):**

| Event | Caller | Notify fn |
|-------|--------|-----------|
| Contact form | `app/api/contact/route.ts` | `notifyAdminsOfContactMessage` |
| Bespoke custom | `app/api/bespoke-requests/stickers/custom/route.ts` | `notifyAdminsOfBespokeRequest` |
| Orders | checkout-bank + stripe paid | `notifyAdminsOfNewOrder` |
| Newsletter / community / fundraising | respective API routes | matching `notifyAdminsOf*` |

**Recipients:** `ADMIN_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL` → else `CONTACT_ADMIN_EMAIL` → else `COMPANY_CONTACT.email` (`info@selpic.com.au`). Implemented in `resolveAdminNotificationRecipients()`.

**Wave 3 local change:** only adds `requestSummary` as email **bodyText** for Bespoke. Does **not** change recipients, Resend call, or fire-and-forget pattern.

**Failure mode (ops):** Notify is `void notify…()` after a successful save. Customer/API can return **success** while the admin email fails (`RESEND_API_KEY` missing, Resend domain error, etc.) — failure is only `console.warn('[admin-inbound] email failed: …')`. Admin Settings → Email notifications checkboxes are **unrelated** local prefs; they do not gate these alerts.

**Local verify (2026-09):** On `http://localhost:3005/stickers/custom`, Submit shows Submitting…, then success banner + cleared form. API returns `adminNotifyOk: true` when Resend accepts the company alert. Production (`www.selpic.com.au`) does **not** include these UX changes until deployed — testers on prod will still see the old filled form.

**Resend:** Contact and Bespoke **`await`** notify and return `adminNotifyOk` / `adminNotifyError` in the JSON (customer still gets success if save worked). Check Resend Dashboard Logs for `[SELPIC Contact]` / `[SELPIC Bespoke]` to `info@selpic.com.au` (or `ADMIN_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL`).

